/-!
# Infrastructure for the HS five-norm algebra certificate

`MarkedNorm` identifies the literal five-center norm ideal with the ideal
generated by the cyclic norm of the published generator B, using a checked
conjugator on the degree-100 carrier. `GeneratorColumns` proves that finite
left-generator relations suffice for the spanning field of `NormCertificate`.
`ShortRelations` checks thirteen ATLAS word identities on the actual carrier,
and `ShortNorms` adds three cyclic norm relations with their conjugacies proved.
`ActionKernel` extracts spanning elements from a small action, and
`CosetModule` separates the universal fixed-vector kernel argument from the
finite action calculation, allowing nilpotence at both stages.

These are proved comparison and assembly results. The finite spanning data
and the nilpotence calculation needed to construct `normCertificate` are not
supplied here. In particular no degree-forty exclusion is asserted.

Source: Guralnick--Malle, Classification of 2F-modules I, Proposition 5.1,
HS paragraph, author-preprint p.16; Aschbacher--Smith K.4, printed p.457.
-/
